# vdc signals its own process group with SIGKILL while shutting down
# ("init: Sending signal 9 to service ... process group"). Platform policy grants
# vdc no CAP_KILL, so the self-targeted signal is denied; vdc still exits with
# status 0, so the cleanup is purely best-effort. Silence it.
#
# linkerconfig and odrefresh show the same denial, but both are private platform
# domains invisible to vendor policy and are therefore left as-is.
dontaudit vdc self:capability kill;
